# Mandatory-review paths. See docs/adr for the decisions behind this setup.
#
# CODEOWNERS applies to the *last* matching pattern, so more specific rules
# should stay below more general ones if that behavior is ever relied upon.
# For now these five are independent (non-overlapping) path prefixes.
#
# `crates/duels-eval/**` is here for a different reason from the other four.
# It is not documentation or configuration: it is a shared asset that more than
# one agent's *measured strength* depends on, and a change to it moves every
# one of them at once. Everything else in this repository can be reviewed by
# reading the diff; this crate has to be reviewed by asking "was this
# measured?". The rule exists to stop its behaviour being changed in passing
# inside a PR that is nominally about something else.

docs/**              @kncesarini
.github/**           @kncesarini
data/**              @kncesarini
crates/duels-eval/** @kncesarini
CODEOWNERS           @kncesarini
